710d62caba729b", "evidence/b428d6504dd5f600ebe2a13bdd7b6510aa7d4a17-1/20260924T003121Z-b556b8b0/setup-0.log": "151dd5920378861c4ae5449003d67330e036201e9293e184a9e6c2c84f4cf393", "evidence/b428d6504dd5f600ebe2a13bdd7b6510aa7d4a17-1/20260924T003121Z-b556b8b0/setup-1.log": "513f5c4c3b1ef1d666f3db7268c689ca5eb3bb040b770e7898e113ff4963290f", "evidence/b428d6504dd5f600ebe2a13bdd7b6510aa7d4a17-1/20260924T003121Z-b556b8b0/setup-2.log": "6c4dd8c62a2d587c5bd70ec8c14f47d2506ab6ea0117388558808800f39acd64", "evidence/b428d6504dd5f600ebe2a13bdd7b6510aa7d4a17-1/20260924T003121Z-b556b8b0/setup-3.log": "70728ece9bedf9dd3fe651f7380640c7f123c28708d88fa10842f1a369ee01ee", "evidence/b428d6504dd5f600ebe2a13bdd7b6510aa7d4a17-1/20260924T003121Z-b556b8b0/setup-4.log": "c187d864d3340d712347db75f9c5fa451c549dce113e99c399f63e37050fe627", "patches/b428d6504dd5f600ebe2a13bdd7b6510aa7d4a17-1/20260924T003121Z-b556b8b0.patch": "ef7ee2b870f66852e79fdab5498092a4dee1baba95f2c06c52e9ac65bb92dcff"}, "expected_failure": "assertion `left == right` failed: input \"00c5a31be2;\" returns Ok with remainder \"e2;\" and value 12952347 instead of Err(Backtrack(...IsA)).", "fixed_commit": "b428d6504dd5f600ebe2a13bdd7b6510aa7d4a17", "fixed_tree": "4c3c3ee32f20280171a4958afa4ac919e58c4b24", "fixes": [{"commit": "b428d6504dd5f600ebe2a13bdd7b6510aa7d4a17", "parent": "e870a6d2d05a7dcc95f871536500f85a9ee61115"}], "patch": "patches/b428d6504dd5f600ebe2a13bdd7b6510aa7d4a17-1/20260924T003121Z-b556b8b0.patch", "provenance": "verbatim", "runs": {}, "test_sources": [{"commit": "b428d6504dd5f600ebe2a13bdd7b6510aa7d4a17", "paths": ["src/character/mod.rs"]}], "tests": ["character::tests::complete::hex_uint_tests"]}, "shard": "winnow", "status": "blocked", "subject": "fix(char): Error on hex_uint overflow", "summary": "hex_uint accepted excessive leading hexadecimal digits by parsing only the first max_nibbles digits and leaving the rest as remainder. For u32, input \"00c5a31be2;\" incorrectly returned Ok((\"e2;\", 12952347)). The fix returns ErrorKind::IsA when the leading hexadecimal sequence exceeds the output type's digit limit. The selected upstream test was updated by this fix to require that error. Both reversal regions occur exactly once in their respective source files.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:34:08.109845+00:00"}
{"commit": "f5c49ba6607517c7eea73a32ffef66515f4b7049", "id": "f5c49ba6607517c7eea73a32ffef66515f4b7049-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Proposal names no upstream test", "repo": "https://github.com/winnow-rs/winnow", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260924T010056Z-ed19d2b4", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/f5c49ba6607517c7eea73a32ffef66515f4b7049-1/20260924T010056Z-ed19d2b4/origin.json": "e4d49ff4cb28b92cf485a7d0d6cb111c375f937b0541de9dc826fcf8ecf6de43", "evidence/f5c49ba6607517c7eea73a32ffef66515f4b7049-1/20260924T010056Z-ed19d2b4/proposal.json": "0068475df3c5fd18742cb6e6aaa3fb8a580f7504cbffdb51a0e5e8aa4faa9b03"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "winnow", "status": "blocked", "subject": "fix(comb)!: Add missing infinite loop check to repeat", "summary": "The count-bounded `repeat(n, parser)` path (`fold_repeat_n_`) had no progress check: if `parser` succeeded without consuming any input, `repeat(n, parser)` silently accumulated n outputs over the same position. The fix adds an `eof_offset` comparison that produces a `ParserError::assert` (debug-build panic, release-build error) when the inner parser doesn't make progress, mirroring the unbounded `repeat0/repeat1` paths.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T01:00:56.296756+00:00"}
